    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "On average, it's about $1.40 per person per meal per day. You can't even buy a cup of coffee with that. So people who aren't SNAP end up going to food banks at the end of the month because they don't have enough to continue to put food on the table for their families. The other thing that has been made clear is that the majority of people on SNAP are children. Our senior citizens are people who are disabled. Of those who can work, the majority work. We had some testimony from people who were working. I mean, they work. They work full-time and they earn so little that they still need to rely on SNAP. So",
