  {
    "episode_id": 72777,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72777.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I do. I will be less than honest with you if I didn't tell you that I think we need to take a hard look at crop insurance. And again, not so much in any way to put at risk any of the small and medium-sized farmers. I mean, I think there is some concern about some of these bigger players that seem to benefit in a way that doesn't always seem fair. But I understand the risk that farmers face each and every day. And we need to make sure that We're there for them in cases of difficulty, which either happens through mother nature or through an economic crisis or through a number of other ways. That's an aspect that I wish we did a couple of hearings on. versus, again, 16 hearings on SNAP. I think there's some other areas that deserve a little attention as well.",
