  {
    "episode_id": 72777,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72777.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "well i i think trade is important but we need to make sure we have good trade agreements that you mentioned after uh... when i first came to congress i represented the city of fall river massachusetts which was by you know a textile center in our country uh... after nafter what was left of the textile industry left and there's been no relief to that city uh... nobody came to help and to invest more as a result of their loss because of that trade agreement and so that's why a lot of people feel anxious when you talk about trade agreements uh... because that may have been good for a small number of people in this country but they're you know a lot of people including a lot of my constituents it wasn't so good you know uh... and the you know they're issues with t p p that that people have raised about dealing with countries like Vietnam, for example, their human rights record, their lack of environmental standards, their low wages, and how do you end up competing on that kind of a playing field? So, look, I think we can do better on trade than we've done. By the way, I've visited with a lot of farmers, not just from Massachusetts, but from all across the country, who tell me that, yeah, I know some of our organizations, favored TPP, But you know what, the more we look into it, the more we're like, yeah, after reservations about that too. So what we should do, I think, is start anew and actually have real people at the table and not just the leaders of big industry or big agriculture, but understand that the strength in this country is with our small and medium sized businesses and as well as our small and medium sized farms. And we need to make sure that their issues are being addressed and taken care of. And I think we can do a better job. So I'm not against trade, but I'm against lousy trade deals. And I think NAFTA was a lousy trade deal. And I think that TPP, as it is written, is a lousy trade deal. And I think We can work together and improve it. We should.",
