  {
    "episode_id": 72777,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72777.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "ever going to Columbia and visiting one of those school feeding programs over a decade ago. And then a young mother. who introduced me to her 11-year-old son, who is being fed and going to school as a result of this program. And she said to me and to the US ambassador, she said, I want you to meet my 11-year-old son. She said, every day one of the armed actors comes through this slum that we're living in. One day it's the left-wing far gorillas. The next day it's the right-wing paramilitaries. And they asked me this 11-year-old boy's mother to give him up, to give him to one of these armed groups. And they say to me, if you give him to us, and he joins our armed cause, we will guarantee him something that you can, and that is we'll feed him every day. And she says, now I don't have to make that choice. Now my son is eating every day, he's learning to read, and hopefully someday get out of this lump. And she says, I thank the American people for that, and I'll never forget it. And I said to the ambassador, I said, that's it. When people appreciate these kinds of programs, when people are grateful, they like you. And when people like you, they don't want to blow you up. We ought to use the American farmers, their ingenuity to help developing countries better develop their agricultural base. We ought to use the food in this country. uh... that uh... that we grow to help feed the hungry around the world uh... this is something that's doable and i believe we could do it my lifetime i just hope we get to the point where we well what we could we can actually talk about solving big problems like hunger at home and hunger abroad and uh... and again i uh... and i'm grateful to the farmers i've met in massachusetts around the country who do so much good and who is so generous uh... They're important to our economy, but more just as important to me is They're one of the reasons why people all over the world respect the United States, so thank you for having me.",
